{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## How the ecosystem handles this — and which option rebar can actually take\n\n### rebar is in the STATEFUL mode, by default rather than by decision\n\n`src/rebar/mcp_server.py:624,645-655` and `src/rebar/_mcp_health.py:310` call\n`mcp.streamable_http_app()` and set NEITHER `stateless_http` nor `json_response`. The SDK's\ndefault is session-managed: `StreamableHTTPSessionManager` mints an `Mcp-Session-Id` and holds\nthe session IN MEMORY, in that process. That is precisely why a container swap 404s every live\nsession — the state cannot exist anywhere but the container that created it.\n\nVerified against the installed SDK in this checkout:\n\n    FastMCP.__init__ accepts stateless_http  -> True\n    Settings fields present                  -> ['json_response', 'stateless_http']\n\nSo the most impactful option is already available and unused.\n\n### The three patterns the ecosystem uses\n\n**1. Stateless mode — the direction the spec itself moved, and the standard answer.** Each HTTP\nrequest is independent, no session id, no server-side state between requests. Round-robin load\nbalancing works, and failover/redeploy is a non-event because there is no session to lose. The\n2026 spec work (SEP-2243, HTTP header standardization for the streamable transport) exists\nspecifically to unpin clients from a single container.\n\n**2. Session affinity / sticky routing.** Keep routing a session's requests to the container that\nowns it until its sessions end, and only then retire it. This is what rebar's retire path\nIMPLIES it is doing — it keeps the old container alive 21 minutes with `docker stop --time 1260`\nand logs a 'graceful SIGTERM self-drain' — but the nginx upstream is switched FIRST, so nothing\ncan reach the old container. The mechanism exists; the routing does not.\n\n**3. Externalized session/event store.** The SDK defines an `EventStore` interface\n(`store_event` / `replay_events_after`) backing `Last-Event-ID` resumption, with an in-memory\nimplementation shipped and Redis-backed ones in the wild. IMPORTANT LIMIT: this gives stream\nRESUMPTION after a dropped connection, not session portability across processes —\n`StreamableHTTPSessionManager` has no way to externalize session state\n(modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk issue #880). So it does NOT by itself survive a container swap.\n\n### Recommendation for rebar\n\n**Stateless mode is the natural fit, and it makes this bug structurally impossible rather than\nmerely less likely.** rebar's tool surface is request/response CRUD over a git-backed store; the\nblue-green architecture is already committed to replacing containers on a 2-minute tick, which is\nfundamentally at odds with in-memory per-container session state.\n\n**What must be checked before flipping it**, and I have NOT verified these:\n- whether any rebar tool depends on server-initiated messages or progress notifications over the\n  session — the long-running gates (`review_plan` at 15-20 min, `verify_completion` at 9-11 min)\n  are the obvious candidates, and if they stream progress, stateless changes their behaviour;\n- whether `run_workflow`'s async run model assumes session continuity;\n- whether the nginx edge and the auth verifier behave identically without `Mcp-Session-Id`.\n\nIf stateless turns out to be unsafe for the gates, the fallback is option 2: swap the upstream\nonly for NEW sessions and keep routing existing session ids to the old container for its retire\nwindow — which would finally make the 21-minute grace period mean what its log message claims.\n\nSources: Google Developers Blog on MCP stateless scaling; Microsoft 'MCP Just Went Stateless';\nSolo.io 'MCP Stateless Spec Changes'; modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk issue #880; MCP Python SDK\nstreamable_http API docs."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787857324526033001,"uuid":"3776eb04-8ee4-4d53-8475-84852c477bcd"}